Compare against ce.below, not only the hazards at `want`, so the readout's own 'Above the courtesy ceiling' test (use > ce.below) can never fire on the default. Also give Stomp its own goal, so the hazard radius stops raising the goal: `stomp: { key: 'gStomp', unit: 'm', label: 'Goal: felt this far away (m)', text: (t) => 'makes a stomp people feel ' + fmtDist(t) + ' away' }`, with DEFAULTS.gStomp = 5 and VALID gStomp num(0.5, 1000). Change the presence test to assert 'least never above the ceiling' unconditionally. Note: the fix commit 3454988 (which landed during this review) caps using hazards at `want` only, so the chip can still disagree when a hazard turns off again at higher effort, and Stomp's goal is still tied to near.

